From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:07:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: identify the successful WebSocket P2P listener event

Retain Info and the complete successful-listener diagnostic after co_spawn,
using the existing ListenAddress key. This address is a local listener,
not a remote peer identity. No listener/transport/capability behavior changes.

Extend the existing actual HTTP listener fixture with exact event/address/
message checks. Pin its owned P2P bind to loopback so wildcard and onion
listener defaults cannot determine which address the assertion observes.
This changes test setup only; no new production option or alias.

Shared eCash HTTP owner. Source-only lint/Ruff/diff checks pass; functional
fixture NOT_RUN and producer NOT_COMPILED. Sealed381/current integration
is unchanged; later group is not an intake-ready validated delivery.

